UTS #39 section 3.1 applies canonical equivalence when testing identifiers
for Allowed characters: <u, combining diaeresis> is Allowed if both parts are,
or if u-diaeresis is. ICU tests the characters as written, so whether
visually identical text passes depends on its encoding (U+0114 is
Restricted, E + U+0306 is Allowed). This patch tests each normalization
segment in its NFD and its NFC form, for both the CHAR_LIMIT check and
restriction-level step 1, using ICU's own normalizers. Drop it once ICU
applies canonical equivalence upstream.

--- a/source/i18n/uspoof_impl.h
+++ b/source/i18n/uspoof_impl.h
@@ -86,6 +86,10 @@
     void getResolvedScriptSetWithout(const UnicodeString& input, UScriptCode script, ScriptSet& result, UErrorCode& status) const;
     void getNumerics(const UnicodeString& input, UnicodeSet& result, UErrorCode& status) const;
     URestrictionLevel getRestrictionLevel(const UnicodeString& input, UErrorCode& status) const;
+
+    // Whether input is within the allowed characters under canonical
+    // equivalence (UTS #39 section 3.1).
+    UBool inProfile(const UnicodeString& input, UErrorCode& status) const;
 
     int32_t findHiddenOverlay(const UnicodeString& input, UErrorCode& status) const;
     bool isIllegalCombiningDotLeadCharacter(UChar32 cp) const;
